# Demucs v4 Quantized ONNX Model Placeholder

This placeholder indicates that the full `demucs_v4_quantized.onnx` model
has not been committed to the repository due to its large size (~50–200 MB).

## How to obtain the model

### Option A — Download from Hugging Face (recommended)
```bash
python scripts/download_demucs.py
# Outputs: public/app/models/demucs_v4_quantized.onnx
```

### Option B — Convert from PyTorch
```bash
pip install demucs torch onnx onnxruntime
python scripts/export_demucs_onnx.py --quantize --output public/app/models/
```

### Option C — Runtime CDN fallback
The app automatically falls back to BSRNN vocal isolation when Demucs is
unavailable. Set `DEMUCS_CDN_URL` in `.env` to load from a private CDN at
runtime (CDN must set `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin`).

## Runtime behaviour without this file
- ml-worker.js logs: `[ml-worker] Demucs unavailable — using BSRNN fallback`
- All other models (BSRNN, RNNoise, Silero VAD) load and function normally
- Processing quality is ~85% of full Demucs+BSRNN ensemble

## Expected model spec
- Input:  `input` — float32[1, 2, samples] (stereo PCM at 44100 Hz)
- Output: `vocal_mask` — float32[1, halfBins] OR `output` — float32[1, 2, samples]
- ONNX opset: 17
- Quantized INT8 for browser performance
